its} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives of the reciprocal hyperbolic functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(sech x) &= -sech x\\tanh x \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}(csch x) &= -csch x\\coth x \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\coth x) &= -csch^{2} x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use these results to find the derivative of\n\n$$\ny= \\sech x - 2\\csch x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating term-by-term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(sech x - 2csch x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(sech x) + \\frac{d}{dx}(-2csch x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(sech x) - 2\\frac{d}{dx}(csch x) \\\\\n&=-sech x\\tanh x - 2(-csch x\\coth x) \\\\\n&=-sech x\\tanh x + 2csch x\\coth x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535549 17592186045417 false] [17592186168090 1064 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe derivatives of the reciprocal hyperbolic functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x) & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) & =-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use these results to find the derivative of \n\n$$\ny= \\sech x - 2\\csch x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating term-by-term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535549 17592186045417 true] [17592186168101 1064 "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nWe wish to prove the following result:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\sech{x}) = -\\sech{x} \\tanh{x}\n$$\n\nTo do this, we can use the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sech x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cosh x}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equation using the chain rule, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(sech x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{1}{\\cosh x}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(\\cosh x)^{-1} \\\\\n&= - (\\cosh x)^{-2} \\cdot (\\cosh x)^{′} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\cosh^{2} x} \\cdot \\sinh x \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\cosh x} \\cdot \\frac{\\sinh x}{\\cosh x} \\\\\n&=-sech x\\tanh x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can prove the results for the derivatives of the hyperbolic cosecant and cotangent in a similar way." 13194139535549 17592186045417 false] [17592186168101 1064 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$ \n\nWe wish to prove the following result:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\sech{x}) = -\\sech{x} \\tanh{x}.\n$$\n\nTo do this, we can use the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sech x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cosh x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equation using the chain rule, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)}^{-1} \\\\  & =-{(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)}^{-2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can prove the results for the derivatives of the hyperbolic cosecant and cotangent in a similar way." 13194139535549 17592186045417 true] [17592186171932 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515522 13194139535549 17592186045417 true] [17592186185496 1078 #edb/ref 17592186185497 13194139535549 17592186045417 true] [17592186185508 1078 #edb/ref 17592186185511 13194139535549 17592186045417 true] [17592186188276 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515528 13194139535549 17592186045417 true] [17592186188276 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515546 13194139535549 17592186045417 true] [17592186188296 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515544 13194139535549 17592186045417 true] [17592186188536 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535549 17592186045417 true] [17592186188536 1071 "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $E[Y]$.\n\n| $f$ | $Y = 0$ | $Y = 1$ | $Y = 2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 0$ 